Two corrections from review of "[PATCH v3] jails/instances/lab-mail:
Initial spec" [1], each turned into a rule so it does not recur.

Patch 1 keeps earlier quote levels in replies. Replies cut whole
indentation levels, so an answer could sit under a question whose
subject was gone. The rule now says to trim vertically, never
horizontally, and that each message must read on its own.

Patch 2 says to ask pkg before calling a package missing. I reported
notmuch-emacs as not installed because (require 'notmuch) failed
under emacs -Q, without checking pkg. It was installed.

